* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.ENTRIES
*
*   For the administrator only (it is refused, before anything is read, for anyone else; it is in SDSYS's VOC only).  A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43
*   lines at least).  Nothing is copied: every list is read from the account's own file by its pathname when it is asked for.
*
*     Accounts   every registered account but SDSYS with the edit gates it holds (voc-edit, dict-edit, bp-edit, shown as v d b or a dash), whether the sdsys user is in its group, and
*                whether it is suspended
*     Entries    the VOC of the account under the cursor: each entry's id, its type and what it points at, in name order; K switches to the DICTIONARY ITEMS of its files (the
*                dictionary each file pointer of the VOC names): file, item id, type and column heading, in file and id order
*
*   The VOC of an account is read when the cursor comes to the account, not at the start: a system with many accounts is not read as a whole.  F finds an id, or a part of one, in the
*   VOC of EVERY account (this reads them all and is asked for by name); the boxes then list the hits with their accounts, and Enter on a hit goes to that entry in its account.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down, PgUp and PgDn move in the box, Tab changes box, Enter in Accounts goes to its entries (and on a hit goes to the entry in its account), / filters the entries of the
*   account by a part of the id, F finds an id in every account, K changes the kind, E edits the record under the cursor in the IDE, N makes a new record (its id asked first), D deletes the record under the cursor (its id typed to confirm), C compiles the program under the cursor in its own account (run.in), B debugs it there, Esc takes the
*   find and the filter off, F5 reads again, F1 or ? or a click on a [?] explains the box, Ctrl-Q leaves.  Esc or F10 (or a click on the top row) opens the menu bar when there is nothing
*   to take off.
*
*   WHAT IT CHANGES.  Nothing itself: E and N give the terminal to the IDE on the record, in the account it lives in, and take it back.  The only thing the page writes is the temporary
*   pointer in SDSYS's VOC (an F pointer holding the checked path) that lets the IDE reach the account's file, and it takes it away again.  An administrator passes the edit gates; they are shown because they are what
*   locks the account out of its own files.  THE POINTER RULE (owner, 3 Nov 26): a pointer record is edited like any record of its account, but what a pointer points at is never edited
*   from another account; a dictionary that lies outside the account being listed is refused for E and N, before any pointer is made.  D deletes one record through the file it
*   judged; for a program also its compiled program in the .out file, judged by the same rule (a catalogue entry is left).
*
*   THE GLOBAL CHANGE (G) AND ITS UNDO (U).  G works on the rows shown, never more: a filter or a find must be on.  It asks the field (a number, or heading for a dictionary item;
*   a program's source has no field) and set or replace, then shows ONE box with every account, its count, its first ids and what will be refused; Run writes, account by
*   account, each record in the file it lives in (never a pointer's target: the pointer rule refuses it in the box and again at the write), and a changed program is compiled
*   again in its account by run.in.  There is no name to type (the owner's choice).  The records as they were go to &entries.undo& in SDSYS's account first; U puts back those
*   still exactly as the run left them.  Field 1, the type, is changed on ONE record only, with a warning in the box.  A refusal or a failure in one account does not stop the others.  Audit: master global ... per account; entries undo ... per account.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_entries
$catalog $tool_entries

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

deffun is_grp_member(user,group) calling '!is_grp_member'

   prompt ''

* 10 Nov 26 Windows port: an absolute path is one that starts with @ds or with a drive letter and either slash (as _voc_ref tells them, RELEASE_1.1 189).  Linux tests
*   for a leading /.  A path that does not match is relative to the account's directory.
   abs.pat = "'" : @ds : "'0X" : @vm : "1A':\'0X" : @vm : "1A':/'0X"

   MAXV = 3000                                                  ;* entries read for one account, or hits kept in a find: a VOC is a few hundred; more are not listed, and the page says so

   call $tk_open('tool.entries', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.entries')
   gosub sweep.pointers

   GMAXF = 500                                                   ;* the highest field number G takes
   GMAXT = 120                                                   ;* the longest text G takes (a value, a text to replace and what replaces it)
   UNDOF = '&entries.undo&'                                      ;* the last global change's records as they were: a file of SDSYS's own account (the administrator's), as tool.bulk keeps &bulk.undo&
   MKUNDO = 'create.file &entries.undo&'                         ;* the one command that makes it, shown in a box first
   gosub read.undo.info
   gosub build.keys
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   pnames = 'Accounts' : @fm : 'Entries'

   VIS = 10                                                      ;* rows in a list (the list pane's height less 4: set by get.rects)
   pane = 1
   ac = 1 ; atop = 1                                             ;* the row selected in Accounts, and the first row shown
   ec = 1 ; etop = 1                                             ;* the same in Entries (the hits, in a find)
   an = 0 ; anm = '' ; en = 0 ; enm = '' ; hn = 0               ;* read.all reads both before it fills them (BASIC does not short-circuit)
   ekey = '' ; efile = '' ; hfile = '' ; eout = '' ; hout = '' ; vfail = 0 ; dfail = 0
   kind = 1                                                      ;* 1 the VOC entries, 2 the dictionary items of the account's files, 3 the programs of its program files
   filt = '' ; fnd = ''
   ai.arg = ''
   gen = 0
   msg = ''
   done = 0

   perr = ''
   gosub declare.layout
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, '', '', mr)
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, ao)
      ai.arg = ''
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then ai.arg = ao<5>
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if filt # '' or fnd # '' then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, busy, mr)
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', chg)
            gosub get.rects
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* The key table.  U is offered (enabled) only while the undo file holds a global change that has not been put back (read.undo.info).  Built at the start and again after G and U.
build.keys:
   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'open', 'open', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f6', 'box', 'pane', '', 1)                 ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 move between the boxes on every page (Tab does not)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'filter', 'filter', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f', 'find', 'find', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'k', 'kind', 'kind', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'e', 'edit', 'edit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'new', 'new', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'delete', 'delete', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'compile', 'compile', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'b', 'debug', 'debug', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'g', 'global', 'global', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'u', 'undo', 'undo', '', (if un.have and un.state # 'undone' then 1 else 0))
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* Esc takes the find and the filter off first, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'edit', '&Entry', '&Edit the record in the editor', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'new', '&Entry', '&New record', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delete', '&Entry', '&Delete the record', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'compile', '&Entry', '&Compile the program (in its account)', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'debug', '&Entry', 'De&bug the program (in its account)', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'global', '&Entry', '&Global change of every row shown', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'undo', '&Entry', '&Undo the last global change', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'open', '&Entry', '&Open the row', '', '')    ;* S.180: every key's action is on a menu (Enter)
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'pane', '&View', '&Switch box', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'filter', '&View', '&Filter the entries by id', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'find', '&View', 'F&ind an id in every account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'kind', '&View', '&Kind: VOC entries or dictionary items', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this box', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * The AI line: offered the actions that only change what is shown; a proposal is carried out by the page's own key, and its argument is the DEFAULT of the page's own prompt.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'pane', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'filter', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'find', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'kind', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   * G and U are NOT offered to the AI (S.97: no destructive action on an administrator page without the owner's word for that row)
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the system says

* Every registered account but SDSYS by name, with its path, the edit gates it holds, whether the sdsys user is in its group and whether it is suspended; then the VOC of the
* selected account.  The selection is kept by name through a refresh.  The account's own record is the only thing read for the list: no VOC is opened here.
read.all:
   old.acct = (if ac >= 1 and ac <= an then anm<ac> else '')
   names = ''
   apath = ''
   agate = ''
   asds = ''
   asus = ''
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 9
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         if upcase(id) # 'SDSYS' then          ;* 10 Nov 26 Windows port: the register's ids are upper case
            read arec from acc.f, id then
               locate id in names<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                  ins id before names<lp>
                  ins parse.pathname.tokens(arec<1>) before apath<lp>
                  gset = (if upcase(trim(arec<ACC$VOC.EDIT>)) = 'YES' then 'v' else '-')
                  gset := (if upcase(trim(arec<ACC$DICT.EDIT>)) = 'YES' then 'd' else '-')
                  gset := (if upcase(trim(arec<ACC$BP.EDIT>)) = 'YES' then 'b' else '-')
                  ins gset before agate<lp>
                  sg.grp = trim(arec<ACC$GROUP>)
                  gosub sdsys.state
                  ins sdw before asds<lp>
                  stw = ''
                  if upcase(trim(arec<ACC$SUSPENDED>)) = 'SUSPENDED' then stw = 'suspended'
                  ins stw before asus<lp>
               end
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   an = dcount(names, @fm)
   anm = names
   ac = 1
   if old.acct # '' then
      locate old.acct in anm<1> setting op then ac = op
   end
   if ac > an then ac = an
   if ac < 1 then ac = 1
   if fnd # '' then gosub run.find
   gosub read.entries
   return

* The selected account's entries of the kind shown (the VOC, or the dictionary items of its files), read by the pathname the register gives, in name order: ekey (the sort key), enm (the
* id), efile (the file, for a dictionary item), ety (the type word), esm (what it points at, or the heading), en; filt, if set, keeps what holds it.  vfail is 1 when the account's VOC
* could not be opened; dfail is the number of dictionaries that could not be opened; etrunc when MAXV were listed and there were more; eall is the number read.
read.entries:
   old.e = (if ec >= 1 and ec <= en and fnd = '' then ekey<ec> else '')
   ekey = '' ; enm = '' ; efile = '' ; ety = '' ; esm = '' ; eout = ''
   en = 0 ; eall = 0 ; etrunc = 0 ; vfail = 0 ; dfail = 0
   if an > 0 then
      ca = ac
      pat = filt
      gosub collect.account
      ekey = ckey ; enm = cid ; efile = cfile ; ety = cty2 ; esm = csm2 ; eout = cout
      en = cn ; eall = rcount ; etrunc = ctrunc ; vfail = cfail ; dfail = cdfail
   end
   if fnd = '' then
      ec = 1
      if old.e # '' then
         locate old.e in ekey<1> setting op then ec = op
      end
      if ec > en then ec = en
      if ec < 1 then ec = 1
   end
   gosub keep.tops
   return

* The entries of account number ca of the kind shown that hold the text pat ('' = all), sorted by key.  Out: ckey, cid, cfile ('' for a VOC entry), cty2, csm2, cn; rcount (how many were
* read), ctrunc (MAXV were kept and there were more), cfail (the VOC could not be opened), cdfail (dictionaries that could not be opened).  The VOC is opened by the pathname the register
* gives and the records are only read.  A dictionary item holds the text in its id or in its heading.  The dictionary path of a file pointer is read as LOGTO reads a pathname: the
* tokens are expanded (@SDSYS/voc.dic is the system's dictionary of the VOC, and the shipped pointers of every VOC use it), and a path that is still relative is the account's.
collect.account:
   ckey = '' ; cid = '' ; cfile = '' ; cty2 = '' ; csm2 = '' ; cout = '' ; cn = 0 ; rcount = 0 ; ctrunc = 0 ; cfail = 0 ; cdfail = 0
   openpath apath<ca>:@ds:'voc' to vf else
      cfail = 1
      return
   end
   select vf to 9
   if kind = 1 then
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         rcount += 1
         if pat = '' or index(upcase(id), upcase(pat), 1) > 0 then
            if cn >= MAXV then
               ctrunc = 1
            end else
               read r from vf, id then
                  gosub classify
                  locate id in ckey<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                     ins id before ckey<lp>
                     ins id before cid<lp>
                     ins '' before cfile<lp>
                     ins cty before cty2<lp>
                     ins csm before csm2<lp>
                     ins coutf before cout<lp>
                     cn += 1
                  end
               end
            end
         end
      repeat
      close vf
      return
   end
   if kind = 3 then
      * programs: the program files of this VOC, found as tool.catalog finds them (a directory file named bp, or ending .bp, or with a file of the same name and .out beside it, where BASIC
      * puts the compiled programs), then the records of each; a program is built when its compiled program is in the .out file under the same name
      pfiles = '' ; ppaths = '' ; popaths = ''
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         read r from vf, id then
            if upcase(trim(r<1>))[1, 1] = 'F' then
               tl = downcase(id)
               isp = 0
               orr = ''
               if not(len(tl) > 4 and tl[len(tl) - 3, 4] = '.out') then
                  if tl = 'bp' then isp = 1
                  if len(tl) > 3 and tl[len(tl) - 2, 3] = '.bp' then isp = 1
                  read orr from vf, id : '.out' else orr = ''
                  if not(isp) and upcase(trim(orr<1>))[1, 1] = 'F' then isp = 1
               end
               if isp then
                  locate id in pfiles<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                     ins id before pfiles<lp>
                     ins trim(r<2>) before ppaths<lp>
                     ins (if upcase(trim(orr<1>))[1, 1] = 'F' then trim(orr<2>) else '') before popaths<lp>
                  end
               end
            end
         end
      repeat
      close vf
      for fi = 1 to dcount(pfiles, @fm)
         pp = parse.pathname.tokens(ppaths<fi>)
         if not(pp matches abs.pat) then pp = apath<ca> : @ds : pp
         tp = pp
         gosub out.test                                              ;* a program file outside this account is not this account's to edit
         poutf = is.out
         onames = ''
         if popaths<fi> # '' then
            op2 = parse.pathname.tokens(popaths<fi>)
            if not(op2 matches abs.pat) then op2 = apath<ca> : @ds : op2
         end else
            op2 = pp : '.out'                                        ;* this VOC names no .out file (a program file reached by a pointer from another account's VOC has none): the one BASIC makes BESIDE the program file
         end
         openpath op2 to ofv then
            select ofv to 9
            readlist onames from 9 else onames = ''
            close ofv
         end
         onames = downcase(onames)
         openpath pp to pfv then
            if fileinfo(pfv, FL$TYPE) = FL$TYPE.DIR then
               select pfv to 9
               loop
                  readnext pid from 9 else exit
                  rcount += 1
                  if pat = '' or index(upcase(pid), upcase(pat), 1) > 0 then
                     if cn >= MAXV then
                        ctrunc = 1
                     end else
                        pk = pfiles<fi> : '*' : pid
                        locate pk in ckey<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                           built = '-'
                           locate downcase(pid) in onames<1> setting op3 then built = 'yes'
                           ins pk before ckey<lp>
                           ins pid before cid<lp>
                           ins pfiles<fi> before cfile<lp>
                           ins built before cty2<lp>
                           ins pp before csm2<lp>
                           ins poutf before cout<lp>
                           cn += 1
                        end
                     end
                  end
               repeat
            end
            close pfv
         end else
            cdfail += 1
         end
      next fi
      return
   end
   * dictionaries: the files of this VOC that have one (field 3 of the file pointer), then the items of each
   dfiles = '' ; dpaths = ''
   loop
      readnext id from 9 else exit
      read r from vf, id then
         if upcase(trim(r<1>))[1, 1] = 'F' and trim(r<3>) # '' then
            locate id in dfiles<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
               ins id before dfiles<lp>
               ins trim(r<3>) before dpaths<lp>
            end
         end
      end
   repeat
   close vf
   for fi = 1 to dcount(dfiles, @fm)
      dp = parse.pathname.tokens(dpaths<fi>)                      ;* @SDSYS/voc.dic and the like, as LOGTO and the VOC pointers read them
      if not(dp matches abs.pat) then dp = apath<ca> : @ds : dp
      tp = dp
      gosub out.test                                              ;* a dictionary outside this account (SDSYS's voc.dic, which every account's pointer shares, or another account's) is not this account's to edit
      doutf = is.out
      openpath dp to df then
         select df to 9
         loop
            readnext did from 9 else exit
            rcount += 1
            read dr from df, did then
               gosub dclassify
               match.it = (pat = '')
               if not(match.it) then match.it = (index(upcase(did), upcase(pat), 1) > 0 or index(upcase(dhead), upcase(pat), 1) > 0)
               if match.it then
                  if cn >= MAXV then
                     ctrunc = 1
                  end else
                     dk = dfiles<fi> : '*' : did
                     locate dk in ckey<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                        ins dk before ckey<lp>
                        ins did before cid<lp>
                        ins dfiles<fi> before cfile<lp>
                        ins dty before cty2<lp>
                        ins dhead before csm2<lp>
                        ins doutf before cout<lp>
                        cn += 1
                     end
                  end
               end
            end
         repeat
         close df
      end else
         cdfail += 1
      end
   next fi
   return

* In: tp (a pathname with its tokens expanded and made absolute), ca (the account number).  Out: is.out, 1 when the path lies OUTSIDE the directory of that account, whether in SDSYS, in
* another account or anywhere else.  THE OWNER'S RULE (3 Nov 26, in three messages): "pointers back to sdsys should not be editable ... they need to be edited in the sdsys account"; then
* "the actual pointer should be editable, for example change @SDSYS/voc.dic to some other directory.  But the system should not follow and edit something in SDSYS from another account";
* then "no pointer records should ever allow the master to end up editing something in [one] account from [another].  The actual pointer could be edited but never the target of the
* pointer."  So a row marked > means, for a VOC entry, that the POINTER leads outside this account (the record is this account's and is edited like any VOC entry; what it points at is
* never reached from here) and, for a dictionary item, that the ITEM LIVES OUTSIDE this account (read through its pointer; it is edited in the account it lives in).  The question is
* the kernel's own geometry (K$PATH.IN: realpath, so .. and links cannot make a path look inside).  This stage edits nothing; the stages that edit follow the rule.
out.test:
   is.out = (if kernel(K$PATH.IN, apath<ca> : @fm : tp) then 0 else 1)
   return

* In: dr (a dictionary item).  Out: dty (D, I, E, L, PH or X), dhead (its column heading, or for a phrase and a text what it says), on one line
dclassify:
   t1 = upcase(trim(dr<1>))
   dty = t1[1, 1]
   if t1[1, 2] = 'PH' then dty = 'PH'
   if dty = 'D' or dty = 'I' or dty = 'E' or dty = 'L' then
      dhead = dr<4>
   end else
      dhead = dr<2>
   end
   dhead = convert(@vm, ' ', convert(@sm, ' ', dhead))
   return

* F: the text in the entries of the kind shown of EVERY account (an id for the VOC; an id or a heading for a dictionary item).  The hits are kept in name order of account and key: hacc,
* hid, hfile, hty, hsm, hn; htrunc when there were more than MAXV; hseen is the number of VOCs that could be opened.  This reads every VOC (and every dictionary); it is run only when it is
* asked for, and again by F5.  Each account's entries come back from collect.account already sorted, and the accounts are taken in name order, so the hits are appended.
run.find:
   hacc = '' ; hid = '' ; hfile = '' ; hty = '' ; hsm = '' ; hout = '' ; hn = 0 ; htrunc = 0 ; hseen = 0
   for a = 1 to an
      ca = a
      pat = fnd
      gosub collect.account
      if not(cfail) then
         hseen += 1
         for q = 1 to cn
            if hn >= MAXV then
               htrunc = 1
            end else
               hn += 1
               hacc<hn> = anm<a>
               hid<hn> = cid<q>
               hfile<hn> = cfile<q>
               hty<hn> = cty2<q>
               hsm<hn> = csm2<q>
               hout<hn> = cout<q>
            end
         next q
         if ctrunc then htrunc = 1
      end
   next a
   ec = 1 ; etop = 1
   return

* In: r (the record).  Out: cty (the type word), csm (what it points at, on one line)
classify:
   t1 = upcase(trim(r<1>))
   cty = t1[1, 1]
   if t1[1, 2] = 'PA' or t1[1, 2] = 'PH' or t1[1, 2] = 'PQ' then cty = t1[1, 2]
   begin case
      case cty = 'V'
         csm = r<2> : ' ' : r<3>
      case cty = 'K'
         csm = 'a query keyword'
      case cty = 'F'
         csm = 'data ' : r<2> : (if r<3> # '' then '  dict ' : r<3> else '')
      case cty = 'Q'
         csm = 'file ' : r<3> : ' in the account ' : r<2>
      case cty = 'R'
         csm = 'record ' : r<3> : ' of ' : r<2>
      case 1
         csm = r<2>
   end case
   csm = convert(@vm, ' ', convert(@sm, ' ', csm))
   * >: a pointer whose target lies outside this account - a file pointer whose data or dictionary path leads outside its directory, a Q-pointer to any other account, a remote item (R),
   * whose file this page does not follow to see where it lives.  The pointer record is this account's (see out.test).
   coutf = 0
   begin case
      case cty = 'F'
         tp = parse.pathname.tokens(trim(r<2>))
         if not(tp matches abs.pat) then tp = apath<ca> : @ds : tp
         gosub out.test
         coutf = is.out
         if not(coutf) and trim(r<3>) # '' then
            tp = parse.pathname.tokens(trim(r<3>))
            if not(tp matches abs.pat) then tp = apath<ca> : @ds : tp
            gosub out.test
            coutf = is.out
         end
      case cty = 'Q'
         coutf = (if downcase(trim(r<2>)) = downcase(anm<ca>) then 0 else 1)
      case cty = 'R'
         coutf = 1
   end case
   return

* The first row shown in each box follows the selection
keep.tops:
   if ac < atop then atop = ac
   if ac > atop + VIS - 1 then atop = ac - VIS + 1
   if atop < 1 then atop = 1
   if ec < etop then etop = ec
   if ec > etop + VIS - 1 then etop = ec - VIS + 1
   if etop < 1 then etop = 1
   return

